# CI-05: aws_security_group.ecs_tasks' egress is open to 0.0.0.0/0 (security_groups.tf),
# and is deliberately NOT narrowed. ECS tasks need to reach Supabase, the payment providers
# (Razorpay/Stripe) and every exchange ccxt talks to -- all at IP ranges this account does
# not control and cannot practically enumerate by CIDR. Narrowing this blind risks silently
# breaking live production connectivity, which this remediation effort has consistently
# avoided elsewhere (see INF-02, SEC-17) by designing against real evidence rather than
# guessing. Reviewed and explicitly accepted rather than left as an undocumented failure;
# revisit if/when real VPC Flow Log data makes a precise destination list possible.
#
# The other three security groups this same check used to flag (alb, and both redis
# groups, in security_groups.tf and redis-only/main.tf) are fixed for real, not ignored --
# see their own inline comments.
AWS-0104

# CI-05 / SEC-17: alb.tf's aws_lb_listener.http has no HTTPS counterpart when
# enable_custom_domain=false (the default). This is NOT an unexamined gap: the resource's
# own lifecycle.precondition already refuses to apply at all in a prod/production
# environment unless enable_custom_domain=true, specifically so this exact scenario cannot
# reach a real production apply by accident (see alb.tf's own SC-7 comment). SEC-17's own
# ledger entry already investigated the real, currently-deployed ALB in depth: it has no
# HTTPS listener either, CloudFront terminates TLS at the edge for all real traffic, and
# SEC-17's own fix already restricted the ALB's security group so only CloudFront's edge
# network can reach it directly -- the plaintext CloudFront-to-origin hop this finding is
# ultimately about is the specific, already-identified residual SEC-17's own text names
# ("leaves CloudFront-to-origin traffic as HTTP... until that deeper fix lands"). The real
# fix needs an actual domain name and ACM certificate, a business/ops decision this
# repository cannot make for itself. Reviewed and explicitly accepted, not silently ignored.
AWS-0054
